@POINS. I am your shadow, my lord; I'll follow you.

@PRINCE. Sirrah, you boy, and Bardolph, no word to your master that
I am yet come to town. There's for your silence.

@BARDOLPH. I have no tongue, sir.

@PAGE. And for mine, sir, I will govern it.

@PRINCE. Fare you well; go. {Exeunt BARDOLPH and PAGE}
This Doll Tearsheet should be some road.

@POINS. I warrant you, as common as the way between Saint Albans and
London.

@PRINCE. How might we see Falstaff bestow himself to-night in his true colours, and not ourselves be seen?

@POINS. Put on two leathern jerkins and aprons, and wait upon him at his table as drawers.

@PRINCE. From a god to a bull? A heavy descension! It was Jove's
case. From a prince to a prentice? A low transformation! That shall be mine; for in everything the purpose must weigh with the folly. Follow me, Ned.

[Exeunt]

# Henry IV, Part 2 · Act II, Scene 4

[London. The Boar's Head Tavern in Eastcheap]

[Enter FRANCIS and another DRAWER]

@FRANCIS. What the devil hast thou brought there-apple-johns? Thou knowest Sir John cannot endure an apple-john.

